# Page objects

- Prefer the `page-object-author` skill when adding or extending page objects.
- E2E and integ specs must use page objects—do not inline `data-testid` strings in specs.
- Keep selectors and navigation in the page object; keep scenario orchestration in the spec.
- Auth helpers stay in `*/support/login.ts` (not page objects). Use API login unless testing login UX.

## Cypress (`cypress/pages/`)

- Static class with selector constants + `visit` / action helpers.
- Specs: `cy.get(LoginPage.error)`, `ShopPage.visit()`.

## Playwright (`playwright/pages/*.page.ts`)

- Instance class taking `Page`; methods for `goto`, actions, and `expect*` assertions.
- Specs: `const shop = new ShopPage(page); await shop.goto(); await shop.expectLoaded();`.

## Naming

| Surface | Cypress | Playwright |
| ------- | ------- | ---------- |
| Login | `pages/login.ts` → `LoginPage` | `pages/login.page.ts` → `LoginPage` |
| Shell/nav | `pages/shell.ts` → `Shell` | `pages/shell.page.ts` → `ShellPage` |
| Shop / cart / orders | same pattern | same pattern |

Extend an existing page object before creating a new file. Mirror Cypress and Playwright when both frameworks cover the flow.
